{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/970102-saved-by-the-huntsman","id":970102,"title":"Saved By the Huntsman","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-15T12:22:42-07:00","id":970102,"title":"Saved By the Huntsman","content":"I just thought of something ironic. Given that the Huntsmen wants to capture you/target alive, its an incentive to eliminate perceived threats and to protect you from danger, it can't capture you if your dead (I don't think, although raising you from the dead might not be beyond the True Fae's power).<br /> <br /> So i could see a Huntsman who takes out an assassin from a rival court that's stalking you, eliminating evidence of a crime you committed if incarnation could put you beyond its grasp, pushing you out of the way of a speeding train, ect...<br /> <br /> The Huntsmen could be like a weird mix of a Stalker/Guardian Angel/Bounty Hunter trying capture you, but keeping you safe until it can nab you once and for all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T12:32:31-07:00","id":970111,"title":"","content":"Cue really cunning Fairest abusing this to eliminate political rivals.<br /> <br /> Cue really stupid Beasts charging into danger expecting their Huntsman to take care of the problem for them.<br /> <br /> Cue really smart Darklings DOING NOTHING OF THE KIND ARE YOU PEOPLE CRAZY?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T12:38:23-07:00","id":970113,"title":"","content":"I wonder if a Call the Wild Hunt power will be in 2e, where you summon a Huntsman in the hopes that you can get away while it fughts tge current threat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T14:16:30-07:00","id":970209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/970102-saved-by-the-huntsman?p=970113#post970113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if a Call the Wild Hunt power will be in 2e, where you summon a Huntsman in the hopes that you can get away while it fughts tge current threat.</div> </div> </div> </div> I wouldn't be surprised, although its still possible that it summons a True Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T19:19:23-07:00","id":970404,"title":"","content":"I could see a clever Changeling finding out that Huntsmen A is planning on killing them in the hopes of bulling a friend into giving in to Huntsmen A, so the clever Changeling makes sure their own Huntsman, Huntsman B finds out about this, so that Huntsman B kills Huntsman A with its Acadian Weapon, in order to ensure Huntsman A does get in the way of Huntsman B's plans to capture the clever Changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T22:45:04-07:00","id":970509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/970102-saved-by-the-huntsman#post970102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just thought of something ironic. Given that the Huntsmen wants to capture you/target alive, its an incentive to eliminate perceived threats and to protect you from danger, it can't capture you if your dead (I don't think, although raising you from the dead might not be beyond the True Fae's power).<br /> <br /> So i could see a Huntsman who takes out an assassin from a rival court that's stalking you, eliminating evidence of a crime you committed if incarnation could put you beyond its grasp, pushing you out of the way of a speeding train, ect...<br /> <br /> The Huntsmen could be like a weird mix of a Stalker/Guardian Angel/Bounty Hunter trying capture you, but keeping you safe until it can nab you once and for all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Congratulations, you're playing the game right.<br /> <br /> (But no, seriously, Huntsmen are fucking tricksy assholes who have no problems muddying the water for practical reasons on several fronts at once. Why just try and grab you when they can try and win your trust-and shake it in everyone else?<br /> <br /> The Huntsmen are, as a majority, not smash and grab enemies. They prefer to isolate their targets and tangle them up, and that often means emotionally and socially.<br /> <br /> Why tie you up when then can just impress on you just how very alone you are, so alone except for them?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T22:53:57-07:00","id":970515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/970102-saved-by-the-huntsman?p=970509#post970509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(But no, seriously, Huntsmen are fucking tricksy assholes who have no problems muddying the water for practical reasons on several fronts at once. Why just try and grab you when they can try and win your trust-and shake it in everyone else?</div> </div> </div> </div>As a point of further elaboration: Notice how the way Approaches work means that the least-invested members of a freehold are the most attractive targets for a Huntsman trying to recoup Yearning losses and the place Huntsmen occupy in the ladder of antagonist escalation means they'll tend to be sent to retrieve high-ranking Courtiers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T23:49:10-07:00","id":971187,"title":"","content":"Where do I find information about Huntsmen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T06:11:29-07:00","id":971284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832066-2e-playtest-compilation-now-with-pledges-and-huntsmen\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832066-2e-playtest-compilation-now-with-pledges-and-huntsmen\"> 2E Playtest Compilation (now with Pledges and Huntsmen) - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832066-2e-playtest-compilation-now-with-pledges-and-huntsmen\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832066-2e-playtest-compilation-now-with-pledges-and-huntsmen </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The version I put up yesterday missed the Huntsmen, and then Dave shared pledges, so I've added those. Changeling the Lost 2E Playtest Compilation </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> In this this thread you'll find a playtest compilation v4 for Changeling, it has info on Huntsmen and a ton more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T06:29:45-07:00","id":971292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frishman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/970102-saved-by-the-huntsman?p=970111#post970111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cue really cunning Fairest abusing this to eliminate political rivals.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Really, and here I thought the Free Hold was supposed to be a community!<br /> <br /> Still, I'm hesitant to encourage pissing off a creature who considers existence itself to be painful. Sounds like they don't have much reservations when it comes to getting the job done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T05:54:24-07:00","id":972466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/970102-saved-by-the-huntsman?p=971292#post971292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Really, and here I thought the Free Hold was supposed to be a community!<br /> <br /> Still, I'm hesitant to encourage pissing off a creature who considers existence itself to be painful. Sounds like they don't have much reservations when it comes to getting the job done.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I just read the playtest. So, the Hunstmen are basically andats (from The Long Price Quartet)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T06:00:50-07:00","id":972470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/970102-saved-by-the-huntsman?p=972466#post972466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I just read the playtest. So, the Hunstmen are basically andats (from The Long Price Quartet)?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't know what that is, but the last thing I remember reading about them is that they are neither True Fae, nor Hobgoblins. They're something that the Fae magic into existence and bind into service. The Huntsmen hate self awareness and want nothing more than to go back to non-existence. So when they're created, they seek to fulfill their contract as quickly as possible, so they can die again!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T06:04:08-07:00","id":972471,"title":"","content":"Sure.<br /> <br /> (I don't know what that is.)<br /> <br /> @Nyrufa: Wouldn't be a community without someone being an asshole. It's the people trying to ruin your life that really make a neighborhood cozy.<br /> <br /> But yeah, no, the Huntsmen are fire. Hell, they might be uranium. One does not handle them lightly. That, of course, doesn't stop some people from doing it anyways. Even more bizarre, that doesn't stop some of them succeeding.<br /> <br /> The Huntsmen don't mind too much. The successful are easier to fool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T06:30:41-07:00","id":972480,"title":"","content":"The way I look at it the Huntsmen are made up of completing forces, there living paradoxes (not of the mage kind), all the parts don't like being in the Huntsman state so they yearn to dissolve into their compenant parts, but each compenent has its own driving as well.<br /> <br /> The Arcadian Spirit of the Hunt (unrelated to shadow spirits, its more like the essence of a story about hunting), wants a good sporting hunt instinctively, like a Big Game hunter.<br /> <br /> The True Fae's Breath wants to indulge in the emotion/desires the True Fae was feeling at the time it was breathed into the Huntsmen.<br /> <br /> The pieces of Arcadia wants very by the materials used.<br /> <br /> So just as a human (or changeling) has competing drives, the need for food, sex, water, shelter, security, ect..., the Huntsmen has its own competing drives, which dictate how a Huntsmen hunts and what a Huntsman does while in it spare time, when its waiting for plans to bear fruit.<br /> <br /> Plus Huntsmen have a practical and instintive reasons to use Changeling Approaches, so that adds another layer to their behavior. <br /> <br /> Add to that that they can't deliver you if your dead, then that creates a complicated creature with a singular goal.<br /> <br /> As closest Fae relation, I think that Fetches are the closest to Huntsmen, but their created for very different purposes, with different ingrediants, with different powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}